.TH IOM_INIT 3
.SH NAME
iom_init \- initialize an I/O multiplexing context
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <iom.h>
.PP
.BI "int iom_init(iomux_t* " c ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B iom_init
initializes an I/O multiplexing context structure
.IR c .
This structure is used to manage I/O event notification across multiple threads efficiently.
.PP
The function performs the following steps:
.IP 1. 3
Creates an underlying kernel multiplexing primitive:
.BR epoll (7)
on Linux or
.BR kqueue (2)
on BSD-derived systems.
.IP 2. 3
Initializes internal thread-safe synchronization primitives (semaphores or condition variables) and a queue for storing pending events.
.IP 3. 3
Clears the event queue and sets the context state to idle.
.SH RETURN VALUE
.TP
.B 1
Success; the context is ready for use.
.TP
.B 0
Failure; the kernel primitive could not be created.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR iom_add (3),
.BR iom_wait (3),
.BR iom_abort (3),
.BR epoll (7),
.BR kqueue (2)